🧠 Vision

WebGen AI is a full-stack, containerized solution that generates complete web pages from natural language descriptions using AI (Ollama + Mistral).

It allows users to describe a web interface (e.g., “A login page with username, password, and login button”), and automatically generates HTML/CSS layouts rendered in a live preview.

⚙️ System Architecture

Here’s the full architecture of the system:

┌────────────────────────┐
│       Frontend         │
│  (React + Vite + Nginx)│
│  Port: 8090            │
└────────────┬───────────┘
             │  (REST API call)
             ▼
┌────────────────────────┐
│      Backend API       │
│ (FastAPI / Python)     │
│ Port: 8010             │
│ Routes: /api/generate  │
└────────────┬───────────┘
             │  (JSON HTTP call)
             ▼
┌────────────────────────┐
│      AI Engine         │
│ (Flask / Python)       │
│ Port: 5005             │
│ Routes: /process       │
│ Uses Ollama (Mistral)  │
└────────────┬───────────┘
             │  (Local REST API)
             ▼
┌────────────────────────┐
│        Ollama          │
│ Host service           │
│ Port: 11434            │
│ Model: Mistral         │
└────────────────────────┘

Data Flow:

Frontend → sends description → Backend

Backend → forwards to AI Engine

AI Engine → queries Ollama using Mistral

Ollama → returns generated HTML/CSS + structure

Frontend → displays live result in iframe

🧱 Technology Stack
Component	Technology	Description
Frontend	React + Vite + Nginx	Interactive UI for generation & preview
Backend API	FastAPI	Receives prompts, manages communication between frontend and AI engine
AI Engine	Flask	Sends formatted prompts to Ollama, parses responses
Model	Ollama + Mistral	Generates structured and styled HTML from text
Containerization	Docker + Docker Compose	Isolated, scalable microservice setup
Networking	Docker Bridge Network webnet	Enables inter-service communication
Environment	.env	Controls ports and URLs dynamically
🧩 Ports Configuration
Service	Port (Host)	Port (Container)	Description
Frontend	8090	80	Nginx serving the React app
Backend API	8010	8000	FastAPI REST service
AI Engine	5005	5005	Flask server connected to Ollama
Ollama (Host)**	11434	11434	Model serving endpoint
📁 Key Files
File	Purpose
docker-compose.yml	Defines services and networks
backend-api/main.py	FastAPI bridge
ai-engine/main.py	Flask AI Engine logic
frontend/src/App.jsx	Main React app interface
.env	Contains all configurable URLs and ports
🔧 Environment Configuration (.env)
# Backend
BACKEND_HOST=0.0.0.0
BACKEND_PORT=8010
AI_ENGINE_URL=http://webgen-ai-ai-engine:5005

# AI Engine
AI_ENGINE_HOST=0.0.0.0
AI_ENGINE_PORT=5005
OLLAMA_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434

# Frontend
FRONTEND_PORT=8090
VITE_API_URL=http://51.75.240.22:8010

🐳 Docker Configuration (docker-compose.yml)
version: '3.8'

services:
  backend-api:
    build: ./backend-api
    container_name: webgen-ai-backend-api
    ports:
      - "8010:8000"
    environment:
      - AI_ENGINE_URL=http://webgen-ai-ai-engine:5005
    depends_on:
      - ai-engine
    networks:
      - webnet

  ai-engine:
    build: ./ai-engine
    container_name: webgen-ai-ai-engine
    ports:
      - "5005:5005"
    environment:
      - OLLAMA_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434
    extra_hosts:
      - "host.docker.internal:host-gateway"
    networks:
      - webnet

  frontend:
    build: ./frontend
    container_name: webgen-ai-frontend
    ports:
      - "8090:80"
    depends_on:
      - backend-api
    networks:
      - webnet

networks:
  webnet:
    driver: bridge

🧪 Testing Commands
🧠 Ollama Tests (Host)

Check Ollama is running:

curl http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/tags


Expected output → list of models:

{"models":[{"name":"mistral"}]}

🧱 Docker Lifecycle
🔹 Build all containers
docker compose build --no-cache

🔹 Start all containers (detached)
docker compose up -d

🔹 Stop and remove everything
docker compose down -v

🔹 Rebuild & restart clean
docker compose down -v && docker compose up --build -d

🔹 View logs (live)
docker compose logs -f


Or specific service:

docker compose logs -f backend-api
docker compose logs -f ai-engine
docker compose logs -f frontend

🔹 Check running containers
docker ps --format "table {{.Names}}\t{{.Ports}}\t{{.Status}}"

🔹 Inspect network
docker network inspect webgen-ai_webnet

🌍 Server Connection Commands

If you’re connecting remotely to the deployment server:

ssh melek@51.75.240.22
cd /opt/webgenai/webgen-ai
source .venv/bin/activate

🧾 Testing the Full System
1. Verify backend:
curl http://51.75.240.22:8010


Expected:

{"message": "WebGen AI Backend running"}

2. Verify AI Engine:

From inside the backend container:

docker exec -it webgen-ai-backend-api ping webgen-ai-ai-engine


From host:

curl http://51.75.240.22:5005


Expected:

{"message": "AI Engine running", "ollama_url": "http://host.docker.internal:11434"}

3. Generate via frontend:

Open in your browser:
👉 http://51.75.240.22:8090

Type:

A login page with a blue header, username and password field, and a login button.


Press Generate Screen → HTML output appears on the right panel.

🧠 What the System Does
Feature	Description
🗣️ Natural Language Input	Users describe the web page they want.
🧮 AI-Powered Generation	AI Engine uses Mistral via Ollama to generate HTML & CSS.
💡 Live Preview	The generated code is instantly rendered in an iframe.
🔄 Modular Design	Each component (frontend, backend, AI engine) runs independently.
🐳 Portable	Fully containerized setup deployable on any server.
🔍 Diagnostics & Troubleshooting
Check	Command	Expected
Backend reachable	curl http://localhost:8010	Backend JSON message
AI Engine reachable	curl http://localhost:5005	AI Engine JSON message
Ollama reachable	curl http://localhost:11434/api/tags	List of models
Docker network	docker network inspect webgen-ai_webnet	Backend ↔ AI ↔ Frontend connected
Logs	docker compose logs -f	Watch requests & responses
